WEBVTT

00:03.430 --> 00:05.960
Planetary probe, Voyager.

00:05.960 --> 00:11.620
An unmanned spaceship
that left Earth in 1977.

00:11.620 --> 00:15.910
To this day, it continues to
fly quietly, deep into Space.

00:16.810 --> 00:21.710
The glimmering disk on its outer hull is
a gift to intelligent extraterrestrials:

00:21.710 --> 00:24.480
a super-compilation album.

00:24.480 --> 00:28.560
On it are greetings in many
languages, sounds of nature,

00:28.560 --> 00:31.570
and recordings of humanity's greatest music,

00:31.570 --> 00:35.280
created by the likes of
Bach, Mozart, and Beethoven.

00:35.280 --> 00:39.640
Its name? The Golden Record!

00:39.170 --> 00:43.370
Record... Record...

02:11.980 --> 02:14.820
Live from
Hamamatsu

02:11.980 --> 02:14.820
Unidentified Flying Objects Spotted Worldwide!

02:12.620 --> 02:14.820
What a day today has been.

02:15.400 --> 02:17.520
One moment, sound
disappeared from the world.

02:17.520 --> 02:22.120
Next, people put on wigs,
murmuring music jargon.

02:22.120 --> 02:30.120
Live from
Hamamatsu

02:22.120 --> 02:30.120
Unidentified flying objects spotted worldwide!

02:22.580 --> 02:26.720
And now, in skies all around the world,
are unidentified flying objects...

02:27.710 --> 02:30.120
People are being taken away!

02:30.450 --> 02:31.080
New York.

02:31.470 --> 02:32.000
Paris.

02:32.290 --> 02:32.880
Moscow.

02:33.180 --> 02:33.750
Beijing.

02:34.030 --> 02:34.750
Rio.

02:34.960 --> 02:36.680
And Hamamatsu.

02:36.680 --> 02:40.260
Just what problem do they
have with these cities?

02:40.260 --> 02:44.260
Unidentified Flying Objects Spotted Worldwide!

02:41.050 --> 02:42.760
What the hell?!

02:42.760 --> 02:44.260
I-It's a curse.

02:44.590 --> 02:46.050
It's not a curse.

02:45.140 --> 02:50.390
25: Encore from the Skies

02:46.050 --> 02:47.180
It's a UFO.

02:47.180 --> 02:48.870
Sure is galactic, huh?

02:48.870 --> 02:50.240
Amazing.

02:50.240 --> 02:52.620
Is everyone okay?

02:52.620 --> 02:53.730
Senpai!

02:54.010 --> 02:55.320
I'm so glad you're safe.

02:55.320 --> 02:56.030
Of course.

02:56.030 --> 02:57.360
My little kitten.

02:58.130 --> 03:00.220
I was so worried about you.

03:00.220 --> 03:03.160
B-But now there's wacky things in the sky.

03:03.360 --> 03:04.540
They're all over the world.

03:04.540 --> 03:05.870
That looks fun!

03:06.420 --> 03:08.120
Hey, Kanae!

03:08.120 --> 03:08.870
Kanae!

03:09.270 --> 03:09.830
Are you there?

03:10.080 --> 03:11.080
Dad?

03:11.390 --> 03:14.210
Hey, looks like you stopped the Octovas.

03:14.210 --> 03:15.590
I knew you could do it, Kanae.

03:16.030 --> 03:18.210
No, like, where are you?

03:18.210 --> 03:19.870
Oh, can you see?

03:19.870 --> 03:22.050
A UFO arrived above my place, too.

03:22.050 --> 03:25.970
I was taking some pictures
for you when it abducted me.

03:27.210 --> 03:27.980
I knew it.

03:27.980 --> 03:29.090
Lucky!

03:29.090 --> 03:30.920
Are the aliens any fun?

03:30.920 --> 03:32.090
I don't know.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.070
They won't show themselves.

03:35.660 --> 03:37.400
But look.

03:37.820 --> 03:39.110
What do you think that is?

03:39.830 --> 03:41.080
A mic?

03:41.080 --> 03:42.700
What, are you going to
sing karaoke or something?

03:42.940 --> 03:44.770
Karaoke, huh?

03:44.770 --> 03:45.870
That makes sense.

03:46.270 --> 03:48.670
Let's see if that idea takes me anywhere.

03:48.670 --> 03:49.320
Later.

03:50.230 --> 03:51.360
Wait.

03:51.360 --> 03:52.670
I knew it.

03:53.650 --> 03:56.440
My suspicions were correct.

03:56.440 --> 03:57.740
Why are you here?

03:57.740 --> 04:00.550
He gave us a ride home in his car.

04:01.180 --> 04:03.300
I have always had the feeling...

04:03.900 --> 04:08.260
That somewhere in the universe,
someone was listening to my music.

04:09.150 --> 04:12.400
I thought they would someday come to Earth...

04:12.820 --> 04:14.400
in search of music.

04:14.660 --> 04:16.070
Music?

04:16.600 --> 04:18.470
In preparation for this day,

04:18.470 --> 04:19.400
I have been preparing

04:19.400 --> 04:23.310
a device to make it possible for people
to communicate through music:

04:23.810 --> 04:26.160
the Octovas.

04:26.810 --> 04:29.940
But I thought Senpai destroyed that device.

04:29.940 --> 04:30.630
Uh-huh.

04:30.630 --> 04:31.990
I helped, too.

04:31.990 --> 04:34.580
It was almost wrecked by
the time we got there.

04:34.850 --> 04:36.750
That won't be an issue.

04:41.570 --> 04:44.890
We've already made emergency repairs.

04:44.890 --> 04:46.800
M-My yard!

04:47.850 --> 04:52.810
My brother and sister ClassicaLoids,
now more than ever, we, the Eight Sounds,

04:53.070 --> 04:57.530
must become one and play
Musik for our alien guests.

04:58.440 --> 04:59.980
Why?

05:00.170 --> 05:03.830
I haven't heard a single thing about aliens.

05:03.830 --> 05:08.110
That's so important. Why didn't you tell us?

05:06.520 --> 05:08.120
You always do this.

05:08.890 --> 05:11.370
Who would have believed me?

05:12.290 --> 05:16.010
You're the one who doesn't
trust anyone, Bach-sama.

05:16.010 --> 05:17.330
Tchaiko-chan...

05:18.020 --> 05:20.670
You suck, Bach-sama!

05:22.040 --> 05:23.670
You made her cry.

05:23.670 --> 05:24.630
You're low.

05:24.630 --> 05:26.400
Something's suspicious about this.

05:26.400 --> 05:27.490
I know, right?

05:27.490 --> 05:28.340
Agreed.

05:28.340 --> 05:31.260
So, when can I get you to fix the yard?

05:32.000 --> 05:34.270
G-Guys...

05:34.880 --> 05:36.730
Don't any of you care about the Earth?

05:39.620 --> 05:41.650
What's gotten into you, Sousuke?

05:41.650 --> 05:43.880
Why did you suddenly jet out of the mansion?

05:43.880 --> 05:45.930
Weren't you listening to what Bach-san said?

05:45.930 --> 05:46.450
What?

05:46.670 --> 05:49.240
This might be my chance to save the world!

05:50.710 --> 05:53.360
Saving the world with my music...

05:53.360 --> 05:55.420
Wouldn't that be badass?

06:05.930 --> 06:08.010
I feel like we should be doing something.

06:08.440 --> 06:09.530
Like, a lot.

06:11.160 --> 06:12.010
Sousuke?

06:13.500 --> 06:14.350
The UFO!

06:14.350 --> 06:15.310
I did it!

06:15.310 --> 06:16.210
What?

06:16.210 --> 06:17.390
You're in the UFO?

06:17.390 --> 06:18.630
Since when?

06:18.630 --> 06:19.690
Lucky.

06:19.690 --> 06:21.750
I think I'll do it.

06:21.750 --> 06:25.690
I'mma use my original songs to become
the bridge between Earth and space.

06:25.960 --> 06:27.650
I think I'll do it!

06:28.780 --> 06:30.570
Do you even have any idea?

06:30.570 --> 06:33.340
Your song could potentially
destroy the world!

06:39.120 --> 06:41.350
Behold, my brothers and sisters.

06:41.350 --> 06:45.410
The tragic conclusion of
inferior communication.

07:06.060 --> 07:10.500
Boo! That's not it!

07:16.280 --> 07:17.620
C-Crapola.

07:18.020 --> 07:20.120
It's happening all over the world.

07:20.500 --> 07:21.490
This is awful.

07:21.490 --> 07:23.820
Sousuke's song is causing this?

07:25.350 --> 07:26.300
My little kitten.

07:27.480 --> 07:28.340
Bach-san.

07:29.140 --> 07:31.720
Humanity has been completely misunderstood.

07:31.940 --> 07:34.450
Is it true what you said earlier?

07:34.450 --> 07:38.350
Can we really become friends with the
aliens if we make music with the Octovas?

07:44.760 --> 07:47.020
Everyone, assemble!

07:47.380 --> 07:49.030
Are you really sure you
don't want to do anything?

07:49.400 --> 07:51.070
What's the point of being ClassicaLoids?

07:51.510 --> 07:54.700
You could be saving the world!

07:56.070 --> 07:57.270
I don't buy it.

07:57.270 --> 07:59.160
I'm not falling for that man's schemes.

08:09.230 --> 08:10.210
N-No.

08:10.540 --> 08:12.220
The mansion...

08:17.340 --> 08:18.970
Guys, please.

08:19.200 --> 08:20.680
Help me.

08:23.620 --> 08:24.730
Sure.

08:25.670 --> 08:27.500
You rarely ask for help.

08:27.500 --> 08:28.940
I'll hear you out.

08:28.940 --> 08:30.750
You ought to aim higher than
just saving the mansion.

08:30.750 --> 08:32.370
Let's save Hamamatsu.

08:32.370 --> 08:35.240
For Hamamatsu, thus for gyoza.

08:35.240 --> 08:38.140
For gyoza, thus for Senpai.

08:38.140 --> 08:41.260
Saving stuff with huge mechs
sounds kind of like a video game.

08:41.260 --> 08:44.290
<i>You</i> should have been the one
to ask from the beginning.

08:44.630 --> 08:45.780
Right?

08:48.080 --> 08:49.420
Guys...

08:59.560 --> 09:01.520
Damn it. Just this once!

09:01.520 --> 09:03.100
I'm expecting a reward.

09:05.640 --> 09:06.460
Um...

09:08.380 --> 09:12.060
Please save my dad along with the planet.

09:15.130 --> 09:16.470
Andante.

09:21.050 --> 09:23.620
Do not be so hasty, friends
of the great expanse.

09:24.520 --> 09:26.320
We are not enemies.

09:27.160 --> 09:31.500
Behold, in the harmonies
woven of the Eight Sounds,

09:31.500 --> 09:34.830
the quintessence of the people of this world.

09:40.480 --> 09:44.410
Let us ring through the souls of our
peers of megaparsecs yonder...

09:44.410 --> 09:48.350
Our Musik!

09:56.320 --> 09:59.510
Let's show them the treasures
of the people of Earth.

09:59.930 --> 10:03.160
What else but the pure heart of a maiden?

10:06.040 --> 10:09.530
Friendship is what's awesome about Earth.

10:09.530 --> 10:13.550
Have some vodka with us,
and you're our friends, too, aliens!

10:16.150 --> 10:17.860
It goes without saying.

10:17.860 --> 10:19.060
Humanity is love.

10:19.060 --> 10:20.580
Love is forgiveness.

10:20.580 --> 10:22.680
That is our essence.

10:24.930 --> 10:27.220
I'm scared of people I don't know,

10:27.220 --> 10:31.620
but you aren't people, so I think we're cool!

10:33.070 --> 10:38.910
Your earnest devotion to the pursuit
of music is worthy of esteem!

10:40.360 --> 10:43.780
Live life like a dream and
shine to your heart's content.

10:44.040 --> 10:47.160
That's what makes us human.

10:50.200 --> 10:52.740
Humanity is defined by its creation of art.

10:52.740 --> 10:54.420
Art is passion.

10:54.420 --> 10:58.260
Thus passion is the essence of humanity!

11:02.240 --> 11:05.930
Friends, welcome to Earth.

11:21.980 --> 11:23.600
They never fail to impress me.

11:30.510 --> 11:31.370
Am I seeing this?

11:31.370 --> 11:34.380
They're spitting out the people they'd
abducted all around the world!

11:33.360 --> 11:36.100
They heard the Musik.

11:36.100 --> 11:38.020
That's why they're sending everyone home.

11:38.650 --> 11:40.760
Then people must be back in Hamamatsu, too.

11:47.470 --> 11:48.180
Huh?

11:58.720 --> 12:01.290
That's as far as makeshift
repairs can take us.

12:07.670 --> 12:09.540
Do it again.

12:09.690 --> 12:11.360
Do it again.

12:11.780 --> 12:13.580
Do it again.

12:13.760 --> 12:15.550
Do it again.

12:15.850 --> 12:17.780
Do it again.

12:17.940 --> 12:19.800
Do it again.

12:20.000 --> 12:21.980
Do it again.

12:22.090 --> 12:24.070
Do it again.

12:24.150 --> 12:25.740
Do it again.

12:25.740 --> 12:28.470
This is getting even worse.

12:26.350 --> 12:27.970
Do it again.

12:28.470 --> 12:29.970
Do it again.

12:35.980 --> 12:38.080
Do it again.

12:38.150 --> 12:39.480
Do it again.

12:40.040 --> 12:41.850
Do it again.

12:42.050 --> 12:43.800
Do it again.

12:43.800 --> 12:46.160
Hurry up!

12:49.840 --> 12:50.910
How barbaric.

12:51.380 --> 12:53.310
I was hoping we'd be buddies.

12:53.310 --> 12:54.370
They lack love.

12:54.950 --> 12:57.390
Hamamatsu... Earth...
It's all going to be destroyed.

12:57.680 --> 12:59.300
This mansion's done for, too.

12:59.300 --> 13:00.460
Not yet.

13:02.420 --> 13:04.340
They heard the Musik.

13:04.890 --> 13:06.590
They're just waiting.

13:07.080 --> 13:08.490
Sousuke.

13:09.550 --> 13:11.960
They aren't enemies.

13:11.960 --> 13:15.100
We got spit out, but we landed softly.
We were totally fine.

13:15.470 --> 13:16.950
Isn't that awesome?

13:16.950 --> 13:18.690
But they're attacking.

13:18.690 --> 13:20.690
They want more Musik.

13:21.260 --> 13:23.470
You know, like after a concert,

13:23.470 --> 13:27.100
when the audience doesn't go home,
and they all clap together like mad.

13:27.100 --> 13:28.190
That's it.

13:28.190 --> 13:29.120
That's it!

13:29.530 --> 13:31.870
But they don't need to demolish buildings.

13:32.120 --> 13:34.630
They're excited. You can't blame them.

13:35.020 --> 13:37.090
I know how they feel.

13:37.090 --> 13:39.870
They probably saved up money
and convinced their parents

13:39.870 --> 13:41.750
and <i>finally</i> came all the way out to hear us.

13:41.750 --> 13:43.080
We can't end now.

13:43.080 --> 13:44.380
They want more!

13:44.700 --> 13:46.250
But the Octovas is broken.

13:46.250 --> 13:48.420
Who cares if the equipment's messed up?

13:48.420 --> 13:50.390
They came all the way out here to see us.

13:50.570 --> 13:52.510
What are we supposed to do?

13:52.510 --> 13:54.770
How are we going to get
our Musik out that far?

13:54.770 --> 13:56.480
With willpower!

14:01.840 --> 14:03.630
An encore, huh?

14:03.630 --> 14:06.360
I hope there's lots of alien chicks.

14:08.060 --> 14:09.150
Seriously?

14:09.150 --> 14:10.580
You'll do it?

14:10.580 --> 14:11.740
Duh.

14:13.560 --> 14:19.500
Welcome! Nice to meet you.
Here's our super fun Musik!

14:27.690 --> 14:29.190
Here it comes.

14:29.190 --> 14:30.090
Is this for real?

14:34.840 --> 14:35.740
Sick!

14:35.740 --> 14:37.230
Take pictures!

14:37.230 --> 14:38.290
Fine, fine.

14:40.420 --> 14:44.130
Wait, what's the point
in transforming Sousuke?

14:44.130 --> 14:46.100
We're going to have him save the Earth.

14:46.100 --> 14:46.690
What?

14:46.990 --> 14:49.010
What? Me?

14:49.010 --> 14:50.700
I'm out of songs, though.

14:50.700 --> 14:52.410
Spare me, man.

14:53.960 --> 14:57.870
Come on, there's no way we
can leave Earth to Sousuke!

15:02.000 --> 15:03.450
All right, fine.

15:03.450 --> 15:05.110
I'll go.

15:05.110 --> 15:06.010
Okay.

15:06.010 --> 15:08.210
We have a plus one.

15:08.630 --> 15:09.470
Very well.

15:12.710 --> 15:16.810
Let us show them our finest encore!

15:36.780 --> 15:39.950
Let's go, Hasshie.

15:39.950 --> 15:42.370
To protect Earth and our home.

15:42.760 --> 15:44.310
You're totally into this.

15:44.310 --> 15:48.780
It surely ought not to be a ClassicaLoid
to last entertain the aliens.

15:49.220 --> 15:51.340
It must be the task of normal Earthlings.

15:51.560 --> 15:55.310
So let them have our music.

15:55.310 --> 15:57.350
You were the one to bring
it up, after all, Sousuke.

15:57.540 --> 15:59.460
You're seriously sending those two?

15:59.460 --> 16:00.160
Are you crazy?

16:00.160 --> 16:03.600
This is like a Level 1 speed
run straight to the last boss.

16:04.010 --> 16:05.020
Aw, hell no.

16:05.270 --> 16:07.110
Earth's fate...

16:07.110 --> 16:08.940
...is in the hands of <i>those</i> two?

16:09.490 --> 16:12.320
Do you mean to say that this
is humanity's decision?

16:12.610 --> 16:15.120
We just can't be arsed
to go ourselves, right?

16:15.120 --> 16:16.580
Call it what you will.

16:18.330 --> 16:21.780
Show us what you got!

16:21.780 --> 16:22.580
Crap!

16:23.070 --> 16:24.500
All right, let's go.

16:25.430 --> 16:29.970
Give them my best Musik!

16:33.490 --> 16:35.960
They're being way too pushy for that encore.

16:35.960 --> 16:36.970
We have to hurry.

16:37.500 --> 16:39.510
Non non, Kanae.

16:39.510 --> 16:42.190
Suspense is an important part of music, too.

16:42.190 --> 16:45.280
That attitude will someday
invoke the wrath of the masses.

16:45.280 --> 16:46.790
Are you sure?

16:50.490 --> 16:52.140
How can you be enjoying this?

16:52.140 --> 16:54.840
I mean, we're about to save the planet.

16:54.840 --> 16:56.540
It's awesome!

17:02.450 --> 17:04.790
I should have live streamed this!

17:04.790 --> 17:07.690
I could have gotten ridiculous views!

17:08.670 --> 17:11.010
That's the Sousuke we know.

17:16.200 --> 17:17.620
Don't be afraid, girl.

17:17.620 --> 17:18.630
I'm fine.

17:18.630 --> 17:21.770
If I ran away now, they'd destroy
the mansion, the city—everything.

17:21.770 --> 17:24.350
Compared to that, nothing scares me.

17:27.440 --> 17:28.690
You've become strong.

17:28.690 --> 17:30.320
Well, of course.

17:30.630 --> 17:32.840
Thanks to us, huh?

17:32.840 --> 17:34.950
Not that I feel grateful.

17:36.700 --> 17:38.370
Let's dive, Lud-kun.

17:38.370 --> 17:39.530
Very well, Wolf.

17:40.170 --> 17:41.360
Are you kidding me?

17:55.040 --> 17:57.140
I thought I was dead.

17:57.140 --> 17:59.430
They seriously treat people like crap.

18:05.370 --> 18:07.550
Hurry!

18:07.550 --> 18:09.610
Hurry!

18:09.790 --> 18:11.650
Hurry!

18:11.650 --> 18:12.350
Beethes-san.

18:12.350 --> 18:13.110
Beethes!

18:13.500 --> 18:17.460
And to end the day, a fantastic song of joy.

18:18.230 --> 18:21.620
Let this Earth hold an encore

18:21.620 --> 18:26.540
to celebrate this new, unlikely friendship.

18:38.590 --> 18:43.850
Spielen wir unsere Musik!

18:45.890 --> 18:46.820
Hello...

18:46.820 --> 18:47.520
...UFO people!

18:47.690 --> 18:49.150
Here we are!

18:50.560 --> 18:53.110
ClassicaLoids in da house!

18:54.050 --> 18:55.920
That was a lot of mischief you made.

18:55.920 --> 18:57.350
Couldn't wait, could you?

18:57.350 --> 18:58.470
Such warm chants...

18:58.470 --> 19:00.170
It must be the love of the cosmos.

19:00.170 --> 19:02.050
Am I good enough for you?

19:04.100 --> 19:07.790
My friends, it was <i>we</i> who
were eager to meet you!

19:49.260 --> 19:50.710
I think they like it.

19:50.960 --> 19:52.570
They like it!

19:52.570 --> 19:54.210
Awesome!

20:06.920 --> 20:09.310
Let's go on a date the next time we meet.

20:12.490 --> 20:16.200
Fate opens the door to friendship thus!

20:42.460 --> 20:44.910
Autograph, please.

20:46.830 --> 20:49.730
I guess we can take it
home and sign it together.

20:50.370 --> 20:52.020
Scribble, scribble, scribble!

20:51.140 --> 20:52.230
Sousuke!

20:52.230 --> 20:54.230
Kagura Sousuke

20:54.620 --> 20:57.320
S-Sousuke's autograph probably
won't do any good.

20:59.450 --> 21:00.070
You're fine with it?

21:21.410 --> 21:26.590
And so the crazy-intense music
nerds from space went home content,

21:26.590 --> 21:28.710
and Earth was saved.

21:29.560 --> 21:32.670
Now, a few weeks later...

21:37.000 --> 21:38.460
Dad.

21:38.460 --> 21:39.820
I totally forgot.

21:40.500 --> 21:42.730
Long time, Kanae.

21:42.730 --> 21:44.320
Have you been worrying about me?

21:45.130 --> 21:48.820
I'm fine. I'm still living happily,
without a care in the world.

21:49.260 --> 21:51.020
Well, that's Dad for you.

21:51.020 --> 21:53.430
I've been thinking these days,

21:53.430 --> 21:57.190
about how those aliens
learned about Earth's music.

21:57.490 --> 22:00.970
I bet they heard that thing on Voyager.

22:00.970 --> 22:03.170
Remember we watched it a long
time ago on TV together?

22:03.660 --> 22:08.220
That spiffy Golden Record
that got taken into space.

22:09.300 --> 22:14.060
We've just now entered into the age we'd
all been dreaming about back in the day.

22:14.740 --> 22:18.440
If we ever have any more guests over,
you'll have to entertain them.

22:19.340 --> 22:22.320
I'm glad you're well, Dad.

22:22.960 --> 22:25.070
Things haven't changed much over here.

22:25.830 --> 22:29.490
Bach-san was burnt out for a while,

22:30.210 --> 22:33.620
but now he's well again,
and back to work producing again.

22:34.190 --> 22:37.620
Tchaiko-chan and Bąda-chan say
Bach-san gave them a reward

22:38.250 --> 22:40.630
for their hard work with the aliens,

22:41.030 --> 22:45.380
in the form of a capable manager,
by which they mean Mitsuru-san.

22:46.010 --> 22:50.390
Beethes, Motes, Liszt-san, Chopin-san
and Schu-san left to travel.

22:51.520 --> 22:53.350
They've been inspired
to go to all the nations

22:53.350 --> 22:56.040
that they sent their Musik
to during the UFO incident.

22:56.040 --> 23:00.440
The mansion's empty now, and Sousuke
looks a bit lonely, I guess.

23:01.590 --> 23:05.710
But I think he's trying his best
to make something of himself.

23:09.350 --> 23:11.660
A street performance with just
one song in your repertoire?

23:11.660 --> 23:13.660
I commend your confidence.

23:14.270 --> 23:17.900
How could you have the gall to make
your debut while we're out on vacation?

23:17.900 --> 23:19.140
Hurry up and get started.

23:19.140 --> 23:22.240
Everyone, listen up.

23:24.330 --> 23:27.070
Now I'm just hoping everyone comes home safe

23:27.070 --> 23:30.180
and brings in a little rent money.

23:30.670 --> 23:31.550
Ladies and gentlemen!

23:31.920 --> 23:36.100
Kagura Sousuke here, from my first station
tour to my second round of performances.

23:36.400 --> 23:37.830
Welcome!

23:37.830 --> 23:39.350
What a short tour.

23:40.420 --> 23:42.140
He sure is relaxed at home.

23:44.030 --> 23:45.610
It's a live show!

23:46.520 --> 23:49.680
Sousuke-sama!

23:56.320 --> 23:57.750
Ah, girl.

23:58.830 --> 24:00.130
It's been a while.

24:00.130 --> 24:04.060
Shall we have your bland miso
soup and my ultimate gyoza?

24:04.980 --> 24:06.670
Kanae, did you miss—

24:07.910 --> 24:09.420
Nope.

24:09.420 --> 24:11.180
I'm not hoping.

24:12.330 --> 24:18.850
Everyone, get out, right now!

24:25.980 --> 24:30.990
Season 2 Airs In October
